--TEST--
Only a number literal is placed at the `decimal` member of a union: an `int` variable stored at `?decimal` does not compile, and `3 as ?decimal` cannot fail, as `3 as ?int` cannot — `rule:types/numeric-literal-placement`
--FILE--
<?nvs
int $count = 3;
?decimal $price = $count;
var $rate = 3 as ?decimal;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `null|decimal`, found `int`
%A
error[E0709]: `decimal as ?decimal` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
